------ English version ------

Dear Professor,

A thesis that you are supervising has just been submitted online in the UClouvain electronic thesis repository.

Attached, you will find the deposit certificate. This document indicates the type of access chosen by the author for their thesis; the details are also reproduced below, along with links allowing you to download the submitted files.

The electronic version submitted by the student constitutes the official version of the defended thesis. In the case of a parallel submission of one or more printed copies for the jury, the student commits to ensuring the exact conformity of both versions. Nevertheless, the supervisor is encouraged to download the submitted files to verify that no errors have been made by the student during submission and, if necessary, to subject them to plagiarism detection software.

Furthermore, we would like to draw your attention to the importance, as the supervisor, of ensuring the appropriateness of the access level chosen by the student. In particular, it is your responsibility to make the student aware of the need to respect any confidentiality clauses that may bind them to third parties under a specific agreement they may have signed (e.g., with a company whose data is cited in the thesis or its appendix/appendices), legal provisions related to copyright (e.g., for the reproduction of images, photographs, or texts), and personal data protection (e.g., interviews, medical data).

To this end, the supervisor is invited to communicate to the faculty administration any restrictions they wish to see applied.

${params[1]}

#if(${params[2]})
Files submitted:
#foreach($url in ${params[2]})
    - ${url}
#end
#end

The ${config.get('dspace.name')} Team.